 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "Germination is the growth of a seed into a seedling. The seed takes in water through the micropyle, swells, the testa splits, the radicle grows down and the plumule grows up.\nConditions needed:\n• water (to soften the testa and start the enzymes that use the stored food);\n• oxygen (air), for respiration to release energy;\n• a suitable temperature (warmth), for the enzymes to work.\nLight is not needed for germination (seeds germinate in the dark soil), but the seedling needs it later to make food.\nTypes of germination:\n• epigeal: the cotyledons are carried above the ground (bean, groundnut, pawpaw);\n• hypogeal: the cotyledons stay below the ground (maize, pea, mango).",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "s": "maize"
  },
  "problem": "Seeds of {s} are planted in dry sand in a warm room. They do not germinate. Explain, and say what must be added.",
  "steps": [
   "Germination needs water, oxygen and warmth.",
   "The sand is dry, so the seeds cannot take in water and start using their stored food.",
   "Water must be added (with air in the soil and warmth already there)."
  ],
  "answer": "No water; add water.",
  "checks": []
 },
